IMPORT prelude

-- Healthcare Services Act 2020 (Singapore) -- what is a healthcare service and a clinical procedure (s 3), who must be licensed
-- and the penalties (ss 5, 8, 9, 9A), the ambulatory surgical centre service (First Schedule), transfer and lapse of a licence
-- (ss 16, 18), employee records (s 28(4)), names and titles (s 29), advertising and the title "Doctor" (ss 31, 31A, 31B), and
-- obstruction and false statements (ss 42, 43).
--
-- Edition: Act 3 of 2020, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HSA2020.txt, with amendments by
-- Act 11 of 2023 (in force 1 May and 26 June 2023), Act 31 of 2022, S 1/2022, S 387/2023 and S 800/2023 (in force 18 December
-- 2023) shown. The deposit's page headers read "NO. 3 OF 2020"; the deposit does not say it is a Revised Edition text.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a clinic, a practitioner or
-- an advertiser meets. Not encoded: the licence and approval application procedure (ss 10 to 11E), licence conditions and
-- modification (ss 13 to 15), security deposits (s 19), regulatory action and its procedure (ss 20, 21) beyond one ground,
-- key appointment holders and committees (ss 23 to 26), step-in orders (Part 4), most enforcement powers (Part 5), appeals
-- (Part 6), the Schedules' definitions other than the ambulatory surgical centre service, and the Second Schedule appointed days
-- (column-shifted in the deposit -- see NOTES.md).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Healthcare Services Act 2020 -- licensing, names and advertising`

§§ `3 -- healthcare service and clinical procedure`

-- s 3(1): "healthcare service" means any of the following services, "whether or not provided for reward": (a) assessment,
-- diagnosis, treatment, prevention or alleviation of an ailment ... affecting any part of the human body or mind; (b) nursing or
-- rehabilitative care of an individual suffering from such an ailment; (c) "conduct of any clinical procedure to change, or that
-- is intended to change, the appearance or anatomy of an individual"; (d) assessment of the health of an individual; (e) any other
-- prescribed service. "licensable healthcare service" means a healthcare service specified in the First Schedule.
GIVEN `treats, diagnoses or prevents an ailment of body or mind` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `nursing or rehabilitative care of the ailing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a clinical procedure to change appearance or anatomy` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `assesses an individual's health` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `prescribed by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `provided for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a healthcare service` IF
        `treats, diagnoses or prevents an ailment of body or mind`
    OR `nursing or rehabilitative care of the ailing`
    OR `a clinical procedure to change appearance or anatomy`
    OR `assesses an individual's health`
    OR `prescribed by regulations`

-- s 3(2): "clinical procedure" (a) means a procedure that ONLY a medical practitioner, a dentist or an oral health therapist is
-- authorised under written law to perform and which involves (i) puncture of the skin to inject ... or withdraw; (ii) penetration of
-- a body orifice; (iii) external application of energy "capable of causing severe or irreversible injury"; (iv) exfoliation that
-- "targets below the epidermis"; (v) manipulation of dental tissues; but (b) "does not include" (i) body piercing; (ii) body
-- tattooing; (iii) application of intense pulsed light.
GIVEN `reserved by law to doctors, dentists or oral health therapists` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `involves a listed bodily intervention` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is piercing, tattooing or intense pulsed light` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a clinical procedure` IF
    `reserved by law to doctors, dentists or oral health therapists`
    AND `involves a listed bodily intervention`
    AND (NOT `is piercing, tattooing or intense pulsed light`)

§§ `First Schedule para 1 -- licensable healthcare services`

-- First Schedule para 1: (a) acute hospital; (b) ambulatory surgical centre; (c) assisted reproduction; (d) blood banking;
-- (e) clinical laboratory; (f) community hospital; (g) contingency care; (h) cord blood banking; (i) emergency ambulance;
-- (j) human tissue banking; (k) medical transport; (l) nuclear medicine; (m) outpatient dental; (n) outpatient medical;
-- (o) outpatient renal dialysis; (p) radiological; (q) nursing home [S 800/2023 wef 18/12/2023]. The last two kinds below are
-- illustrations of services NOT named in the Schedule.
DECLARE ServiceKind IS ONE OF
    `an acute hospital service`
    `an ambulatory surgical centre service`
    `an assisted reproduction service`
    `a blood banking service`
    `a clinical laboratory service`
    `a community hospital service`
    `a contingency care service`
    `a cord blood banking service`
    `an emergency ambulance service`
    `a human tissue banking service`
    `a medical transport service`
    `a nuclear medicine service`
    `an outpatient dental service`
    `an outpatient medical service`
    `an outpatient renal dialysis service`
    `a radiological service`
    `a nursing home service`
    `a traditional Chinese medicine service`
    `a psychological counselling service`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A ServiceKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is licensable` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a traditional Chinese medicine service` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a psychological counselling service` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `First Schedule para 2 -- ambulatory surgical centre service`

-- "relevant procedure": (a) any surgical procedure or (b) any other procedure performed with the administration of anaesthetics,
-- performed on an individual who, at the start, "is not assessed by a medical practitioner or dentist to require accommodation for
-- ... a period exceeding 12 hours after the individual is admitted". "ambulatory surgical centre service" is the provision of such a
-- procedure (and ancillary services) but EXCLUDES: (c) a relevant procedure "that does not require general anaesthesia" by a
-- licensee of a community hospital, contingency care, outpatient dental, outpatient medical or outpatient renal dialysis service;
-- (d) a relevant procedure by an acute hospital licensee to an inpatient; (e) an assisted reproduction procedure by an assisted
-- reproduction licensee; (f) a relevant procedure with anaesthetics by a nuclear medicine or radiological licensee.
DECLARE ProviderLicence IS ONE OF
    `no other licence`
    `an outpatient medical licence`
    `an outpatient dental licence`
    `a community hospital licence`
    `a contingency care licence`
    `an outpatient renal dialysis licence`
    `an acute hospital licence`
    `an assisted reproduction licence`
    `a nuclear medicine or radiological licence`

GIVEN `surgical` IS A BOOLEAN, `with anaesthetics` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours of stay assessed as needed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant procedure` IF
    (`surgical` OR `with anaesthetics`) AND `hours of stay assessed as needed` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `held licence` IS A ProviderLicence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence is an outpatient or community licence` IF
    CONSIDER `held licence`
    WHEN `an outpatient medical licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an outpatient dental licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a community hospital licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contingency care licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an outpatient renal dialysis licence` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `held licence` IS A ProviderLicence,
      `needs general anaesthesia` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with anaesthetics` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `patient is an inpatient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an assisted reproduction procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exclusion applies` IF
       (`the licence is an outpatient or community licence` `held licence` AND (NOT `needs general anaesthesia`))
    OR (`held licence` EQUALS `an acute hospital licence` AND `patient is an inpatient`)
    OR (`held licence` EQUALS `an assisted reproduction licence` AND `is an assisted reproduction procedure`)
    OR (`held licence` EQUALS `a nuclear medicine or radiological licence` AND `with anaesthetics`)

GIVEN `held licence` IS A ProviderLicence,
      `surgical` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with anaesthetics` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `needs general anaesthesia` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `hours of stay assessed as needed` IS A NUMBER,
      `patient is an inpatient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an assisted reproduction procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an ambulatory surgical centre service` IF
    `it is a relevant procedure` `surgical` `with anaesthetics` `hours of stay assessed as needed`
    AND (NOT (`an exclusion applies` `held licence` `needs general anaesthesia` `with anaesthetics` `patient is an inpatient` `is an assisted reproduction procedure`))

§§ `5, 8 -- providing a licensable service without a licence`

-- s 5: "This Act does not apply to or in relation to any healthcare service provided by the Government."
-- s 8(1): a person must not provide a licensable healthcare service unless (a) authorised by a licence or (b) exempt. (2) Fine up to
-- $100,000 or 2 years or both; "if the person has any previous qualifying conviction", up to $200,000 or 2 years or both.
-- (3) "qualifying conviction" includes a conviction under s 5(2) of the repealed Act (the Private Hospitals and Medical Clinics Act).
GIVEN `the kind` IS A ServiceKind,
      `licensed for that service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exempt` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `provided by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unlicensed provision is an offence` IF
    `the kind is licensable` `the kind`
    AND (NOT `provided by the Government`)
    AND (NOT `licensed for that service`)
    AND (NOT `exempt`)

GIVEN `previous conviction under s 8 or the repealed Act s 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 8` MEANS
    IF `previous conviction under s 8 or the repealed Act s 5(2)` THEN 200000 ELSE 100000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 8` MEANS 24

§§ `9, 9A -- premises, conveyances, delivery modes and specified services`

-- s 9(1): a licensee must not provide a licensable service (a) at permanent premises in Singapore that are not approved premises,
-- (b) using a conveyance that is not approved, or (c) by any other service delivery mode not approved under s 11B. (2) First offence
-- up to $50,000 or 12 months or both; with a previous qualifying conviction up to $100,000 or 12 months or both. (3) Qualifying
-- convictions include s 5(2) or (4)(a) of the repealed Act.
GIVEN `at unapproved permanent premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `using an unapproved conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `by an unapproved delivery mode` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee commits a section 9 offence` IF
    `at unapproved permanent premises` OR `using an unapproved conveyance` OR `by an unapproved delivery mode`

GIVEN `previous qualifying conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 9` MEANS
    IF `previous qualifying conviction` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

-- s 9A(2): "Despite holding a licence", a licensee must not provide a specified service unless granted approval under s 11D.
-- (3) Up to $100,000 or 2 years or both; "in the case of a second or subsequent offence", up to $200,000 or 2 years or both.
GIVEN `licensed for the licensable service` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved under section 11D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `providing the specified service is an offence` IF
    `licensed for the licensable service` AND (NOT `approved under section 11D`)

GIVEN `second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 9A` MEANS
    IF `second or subsequent offence` THEN 200000 ELSE 100000

§§ `16, 18 -- transfer and lapse of a licence`

-- s 16(1): a licence and its rights "are not transferable or assignable" unless (a) the licence contains a condition authorising it
-- AND (b) the Director-General consents in writing. (3) A transfer "is void and of no effect" (a) if not capable of transfer; (b) if
-- in breach of a licence condition; (c) if a condition of the consent was contravened before the transfer.
GIVEN `licence has a condition authorising transfer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Director-General consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `transfer breaches a licence condition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a consent condition was contravened beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer is valid` IF
    `licence has a condition authorising transfer`
    AND `Director-General consented in writing`
    AND (NOT `transfer breaches a licence condition`)
    AND (NOT `a consent condition was contravened beforehand`)

-- s 18(1): unless expired or revoked, a licence lapses (a) on the death of an individual licensee, or on a partnership, body corporate
-- or association ceasing to exist; or (b) on the cancellation under s 20(3A) of "the last valid approval" for any premises, conveyance
-- or other service delivery mode. (2) No part of any fee is refunded. (Whether the licence is held by an individual or an entity is
-- folded into one flag: the licensee has died or ceased to exist.)
GIVEN `the licensee has died or ceased to exist` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `approvals cancelled` IS A NUMBER,
      `approvals held` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence lapses` IF
    `the licensee has died or ceased to exist`
    OR (`approvals held` GREATER THAN 0 AND `approvals cancelled` AT LEAST `approvals held`)

§§ `28(4) -- keeping employee records`

-- s 28(4): a section 28 licensee must keep the prescribed information about an individual (a) throughout the employment and (b) "for
-- a period of 2 years following the cessation or termination for any reason" of the employment.
GIVEN `still employed` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since employment ended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the records must still be kept` IF
    `still employed` OR `years since employment ended` AT MOST 2

§§ `29 -- names, terms and titles`

-- s 29(1)(b): a licensee must not use "Singapore" or "National" (or any abbreviation or derivative, in any language) in its name or
-- logo "except with the Director-General's approval". (2A) must not use a term associated with a defined speciality in its name or
-- logo "unless the licensee employs or engages a relevant specialist" to practise it. (2) must not use a misleading term.
-- s 29 creates an offence only for (3) (a non-licensee); a licensee's breach of (1), (2) or (2A) is not an offence under s 29, and
-- s 20(1)(b)(iii) lets the Director-General take regulatory action for "any other provision of this Act, the contravention of which
-- is not an offence".
GIVEN `uses Singapore or National in its name or logo` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has the Director-General's approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a speciality term in its name or logo` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `engages a relevant specialist` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a misleading term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee breaches section 29` IF
       (`uses Singapore or National in its name or logo` AND (NOT `has the Director-General's approval`))
    OR (`uses a speciality term in its name or logo` AND (NOT `engages a relevant specialist`))
    OR `uses a misleading term`

-- s 29(3): a person "that is not a licensee commits an offence" if it uses a prescribed term or name to convey the impression that it
-- provides a service that may be provided only under a licence. (4) Fine up to $10,000 or 12 months or both; continuing offence a
-- further fine up to $1,000 for every day or part of a day after conviction.
GIVEN `is a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `uses a prescribed term` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `to convey that it provides a licensable service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use of the term is an offence` IF
    (NOT `is a licensee`) AND `uses a prescribed term` AND `to convey that it provides a licensable service`

GIVEN `days the offence continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine under section 29(4)` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days the offence continued after conviction`

§§ `31, 31A -- advertising healthcare services`

-- s 31(1): a person must not advertise a licensable healthcare service unless (a) "a licensee authorised to provide that licensable
-- healthcare service" or (b) acting on the authority of that licensee. (3) $20,000 or 12 months or both; $1,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `licensed for the advertised service` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting on a licensee's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `advertising the licensable service is an offence` IF
    (NOT `licensed for the advertised service`) AND (NOT `acting on a licensee's authority`)

-- s 31A(1): a person "must not advertise, or cause to be advertised, any skill or service relating to the treatment of any ailment,
-- disease, injury, infirmity or condition affecting the human body so as to induce any person to seek the advice of or treatment
-- from the advertiser". (2) It does not apply to the advertisement of a licensable healthcare service provided by a licensee,
-- published by the licensee or on its authority. (4) Defence, proved on a balance of probabilities: published ONLY in a technical
-- publication circulating mainly among (a) medical practitioners; (b) dentists; (c) registered nurses, midwives or enrolled nurses;
-- (d) registered pharmacists; (e) holders of licences to sell poisons; (f) persons training to be (a) to (d).
DECLARE Readership IS ONE OF
    `the general public`
    `medical practitioners`
    `dentists`
    `nurses and midwives`
    `pharmacists`
    `poisons licence holders`
    `trainee doctors, dentists, nurses or pharmacists`
    `physiotherapists`
    `traditional Chinese medicine practitioners`

GIVEN `readers` IS A Readership
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the readership is a defence class` IF
    CONSIDER `readers`
    WHEN `the general public` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `physiotherapists` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `traditional Chinese medicine practitioners` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `advertises a treatment skill or service to induce people to seek it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is a licensable service of a licensee advertised with its authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `only in a technical publication` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `readers` IS A Readership
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertiser is guilty under section 31A` IF
    `advertises a treatment skill or service to induce people to seek it`
    AND (NOT `it is a licensable service of a licensee advertised with its authority`)
    AND (NOT (`only in a technical publication` AND `the readership is a defence class` `readers`))

§§ `31B -- the title "Doctor"`

-- s 31B(1): whoever advertises a healthcare service and refers to a person who is NOT a "specified person" by a protected title
-- ("Doctor", or any abbreviation or derivative, in any language) must include (a) the subject's educational qualification for the
-- title "whenever the protected title is used"; (b) where that qualification is not a medical or dental qualification, a disclaimer
-- stating that fact; (c) "where the subject person has a medical or dental qualification", a disclaimer that the subject person does
-- not hold a valid practising certificate. (3) "specified person": an allied health professional, dentist or oral health therapist,
-- medical practitioner, nurse or midwife, optometrist or optician, pharmacist, or traditional Chinese medicine practitioner, in each
-- case registered AND holding a valid practising certificate. (2) $20,000 or 12 months or both.
GIVEN `calls the person Doctor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person is registered with a valid practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `states the qualification each time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the title's qualification is medical or dental` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person holds any medical or dental qualification` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclaims a medical or dental qualification` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclaims a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement complies with section 31B` IF
    (NOT `calls the person Doctor`)
    OR `the person is registered with a valid practising certificate`
    OR (    `states the qualification each time`
        AND (`the title's qualification is medical or dental` OR `disclaims a medical or dental qualification`)
        AND ((NOT `the person holds any medical or dental qualification`) OR `disclaims a practising certificate`))

§§ `42, 43 -- obstruction and false statements`

-- s 42(1)(b): a person who "without reasonable excuse" neglects or refuses to provide information required under the Act commits an
-- offence ($20,000 or 12 months or both). (2) "it is a reasonable excuse ... if doing so might tend to incriminate that person".
GIVEN `refused to provide required information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the answer might incriminate them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the refusal is an offence under section 42` IF
    `refused to provide required information`
    AND (NOT `the answer might incriminate them`)
    AND (NOT `has another reasonable excuse`)

-- s 43: a person who (a) makes a statement or provides information "false or misleading in a material particular" and (b) "knows or
-- ought reasonably to know that, or is reckless as to whether" it is, commits an offence ($20,000 or 12 months or both).
GIVEN `false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew, ought reasonably to have known, or was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the statement is an offence under section 43` IF
    `false or misleading` AND `in a material particular` AND `knew, ought reasonably to have known, or was reckless`
